  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe camcraft-mcp skill table had no row for 20 tools the server registers in `crates/app/src/mcp/`, `edit_machine` (#1162, PR #1223) among them. This adds one row for each, under the section the tool belongs to:\n\n- Section 2 (setups and machines): `edit_machine`, `get_rotary_stack`, `set_setup_nose_to_axis`, `set_setup_post`.\n- Section 3 (fixtures): `locate_part`, `add_builtin_vise`, `set_vise`, `add_accessory`, `set_accessory`, `add_fixture_plate`, `set_fixture_plate`, `detect_plate_grid`, `get_plate_grid`, `place_on_plate`, `add_mod_vise_pair`, `set_mod_jaw`, `refit_mod_vise`.\n- Section 5 (features and alignment): `detect_pockets`, `set_part_axes`, `lay_part_on_points`.\n\nEach row was written from its registration and schema in source (name, required and optional parameters, refusals, undo), not invented. The skill's own tool names now match the server's registered list (71 names, checked by a set diff).\n\n## How it was checked\n\n- Set diff of the names registered in `crates/app/src/mcp/` against the backticked tool names in `SKILL.md`: before 20 missing, after none missing and no extra names.\n- No test pins the skill text (grep of `crates/app/tests` and `xtask` for `SKILL.md` / `camcraft-mcp/SKILL`), so no Rust gate was run; the change is markdown only.\n\n## Process file\n\nYes. `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` is a process file, so `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` goes from 41 to 42 on this branch. Per AGENTS.md, the number is taken at merge time: if another process PR merges first, the merging session takes the next number when it merges main, and the merge comment on #681 names the final number.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The rows were not run against a live server (no `tools/list` call). They are true to source, not to a running build.\n- The skill is not rendered or loaded by any tool; the text is only read by agents.\n\nChangelog: none (docs/process only)\nEffort: low\nBranched from upstream/main (b65413b2, after the v0.18.0 tag).\n\nFixes #1318\n",
